which is originally established by Dr. Burgess

40:52.880 --> 40:54.840
at the Ohio State University.

40:54.840 --> 40:58.200
And this is the mouse model, the key mouse model

40:58.200 --> 41:03.200
that successfully supports the DSMA development,

41:03.480 --> 41:05.360
the eventual approver.

41:05.360 --> 41:08.920
So, this actually is kind of rapidly then a model

41:08.920 --> 41:12.120
that could kind of predict the translatability

41:12.120 --> 41:15.620
for the capsids for the CNS disease implications.

41:17.100 --> 41:20.720
So, we packed all these AV-9 variants

41:20.720 --> 41:23.840
into a CCE AV format,

41:23.840 --> 41:27.800
and then we packed the same human SMM1 gene,

41:27.800 --> 41:29.180
a stethogensma.

41:29.180 --> 41:33.480
So, then we put these vectors into the animal model.

41:33.480 --> 41:37.080
And here I'm going to show you just one dataset,

41:37.080 --> 41:38.560
which is the survival data.

41:38.560 --> 41:40.600
Of course, we test all the other stuff,

41:40.600 --> 41:43.760
like the body weight, the motor functions, everything,

41:43.760 --> 41:45.760
but here just the survival data.

41:45.760 --> 41:48.960
And here you can see the dotted line

41:48.960 --> 41:51.400
represent the non-trading mouse,

41:51.400 --> 41:55.400
and the black line represent the AV-9,

41:55.400 --> 41:57.520
which is similar to Zogesma.

41:57.520 --> 42:00.920
And then here is the AV-901,

42:00.920 --> 42:05.600
which actually from the biodestribution expression data,

42:06.280 --> 42:09.440
we know that this is a liver-detocated capsid,

42:09.440 --> 42:11.880
and it crossed the BBB efficiently,

42:11.880 --> 42:14.400
much more efficiently compared to AV-9,

42:14.400 --> 42:16.920
and actually it transduces our target cell,

42:16.920 --> 42:19.520
which is the modern neuron cell pretty well,

42:19.520 --> 42:24.200
but it didn't rescue the phenotypes in the SMM1 model

42:24.200 --> 42:27.480
compared to AV-9, it doesn't rescue better than AV-9.

42:27.480 --> 42:31.800
And the AV-902, which is also a liver-detocated capsid,

42:31.800 --> 42:34.560
but it didn't cross the BBB more efficiently

42:34.560 --> 42:38.320
compared to AV-9, it actually works very well

42:38.320 --> 42:40.160
on the SMM1 model.

42:40.160 --> 42:42.720
The third and the fourth capsid,

42:42.720 --> 42:45.120
if you still remember the big table,

42:45.120 --> 42:49.840
the three and the four, they are very similar to each other

42:49.840 --> 42:53.720
in terms of the biodestribution or expression profile,

42:53.720 --> 42:58.720
but eventually there are a therapeutic effect

42:59.600 --> 43:01.600
on this model, it's totally different.

43:01.600 --> 43:06.600
The AV-903 is similar or actually worse compared to AV-9,

43:07.440 --> 43:11.800
but the AV-904, that just works perfectly,

43:11.800 --> 43:15.360
even at lower dose, I forgot the exact dose,

43:15.360 --> 43:19.960
but it could be up to a lower dose compared to AV-9,

43:19.960 --> 43:22.120
can still rescue the phenotypes.

43:22.120 --> 43:27.120
So this is very interesting because these two peptides,

43:28.120 --> 43:30.320
as I said, they are all NHP,

43:30.320 --> 43:32.720
they are library directory evolution,

43:32.720 --> 43:35.360
they are top candidates for targeting the CNS,

43:35.360 --> 43:37.760
they are supposed to cross the BBB better,

43:37.760 --> 43:39.800
and they are very similar profiling

43:39.800 --> 43:42.720
all what our preclinic evaluation,

43:42.720 --> 43:45.040
but eventually they are performed totally differently

43:45.040 --> 43:47.000
in the SMM1 models.

43:48.400 --> 43:52.280
And the one more interesting thing is actually three and four,

43:52.280 --> 43:56.480
they contain the same mutations as AV-902,

43:56.520 --> 44:00.560
which in AV-902, these mutations in the VA1

44:00.560 --> 44:02.960
actually resulted in liver detoxing,

44:02.960 --> 44:05.800
but when we combine the top candidates,

44:05.800 --> 44:08.640
the peptide candidates together with this,

44:08.640 --> 44:13.640
we are one mutations, they are not liver detoxing anymore.

44:13.840 --> 44:16.000
So they are talking to each other,

44:16.000 --> 44:19.520
even one is at a VR8, one is at a VR1.

44:19.520 --> 44:22.560
So here is the data and the summary,

44:22.560 --> 44:25.880
it ends up that we have expected or unexpected,

44:25.880 --> 44:28.960
we have two capsules that works better than AV-9,

44:28.960 --> 44:33.080
and two capsules is actually work worse than AV-9.

44:34.520 --> 44:39.520
So I think it is obvious that there are some

44:40.160 --> 44:43.160
like biology behind this phenomena

44:43.160 --> 44:46.240
that we may need to pay a little more attention

44:46.240 --> 44:49.720
or considerations when we talk about capsules engineering.

44:49.720 --> 44:54.720
And I would say our observation may demonstrate

44:54.840 --> 44:58.680
that the importance of the deriving translation capsules

44:58.680 --> 45:00.960
versus the best transducing capsules,

45:00.960 --> 45:03.720
we should always consider everything together,

45:03.720 --> 45:05.960
the structure, the performance,

45:05.960 --> 45:09.600
and we should choose the appropriate animal disease model

45:09.600 --> 45:14.360
to evaluate the real potential for the clinical translation.

45:14.360 --> 45:19.360
